When ICU’s break rules can’t be loaded, Ladybird now segments text
with a fallback that needs no ICU data, and logs that once. V8
has no such fallback: Its JSSegmenter::New() only DCHECKs that
ICU created the break iterator, so it assumes the data is there.
ECMA-402’s Intl.Segmenter constructor has no step that throws for valid
options, so Intl.Segmenter shares the fallback rather than throwing an
error the spec doesn’t allow.
